1
00:00:02,035 --> 00:00:04,061
<i>Previously on</i> Gotham...

2
00:00:05,739 --> 00:00:07,708
We will create a
legacy in this city.

3
00:00:08,509 --> 00:00:12,276
<i>Gotham falls... we rise.</i>

4
00:00:12,346 --> 00:00:13,746
Together.

5
00:00:14,014 --> 00:00:15,573
Why don't you understand?

6
00:00:15,649 --> 00:00:17,140
(grunts) You need me!

7
00:00:17,217 --> 00:00:19,618
I'm the answer to
your life's question!

8
00:00:21,522 --> 00:00:23,354
All this happened because of me,

9
00:00:23,423 --> 00:00:25,153
<i>because people
were trying to hurt me</i>

10
00:00:25,225 --> 00:00:27,490
<i>and the people I care about.</i>

11
00:00:27,561 --> 00:00:31,054
CHANG: <i>With reunification
underway and the bridges being rebuilt,</i>

12
00:00:31,131 --> 00:00:34,590
<i>it is my honor to bestow
upon Captain James Gordon</i>

13
00:00:34,668 --> 00:00:36,398
<i>the title of commissioner.</i>

14
00:00:36,470 --> 00:00:37,747
What do you mean you're leaving?

15
00:00:37,771 --> 00:00:40,172
- Gotham's in good hands.
- Thank you, Bruce.

16
00:00:40,240 --> 00:00:43,335
That you are the only
son that I will ever have.

17
00:00:43,410 --> 00:00:45,379
<i>And I could not be more proud.</i>

18
00:00:53,053 --> 00:00:55,318
(ship horn blowing)

19
00:01:13,807 --> 00:01:15,742
(indistinct chatter)

20
00:01:19,613 --> 00:01:21,844
BRUCE: <i>Alfred...</i>

21
00:01:22,115 --> 00:01:24,516
<i>I'm writing to let
you know I'm okay...</i>

22
00:01:25,586 --> 00:01:29,114
<i>and that you won't hear
from me for some time.</i>

23
00:01:32,593 --> 00:01:35,529
<i>But I will return...</i>

24
00:01:35,596 --> 00:01:38,464
<i>when I know I'm able to
protect the people I love.</i>

25
00:01:40,334 --> 00:01:43,395
<i>When Gotham needs me...</i>

26
00:01:43,470 --> 00:01:45,405
<i>I will return.</i>

27
00:01:46,573 --> 00:01:48,508
♪♪♪♪

28
00:02:01,154 --> 00:02:02,850
(sirens wailing in distance)

29
00:02:07,394 --> 00:02:09,522
GORDON: It began
a few weeks ago.

30
00:02:09,596 --> 00:02:13,158
Someone attacking
the gangs downtown.

31
00:02:13,233 --> 00:02:14,792
No deaths so far, at least.

32
00:02:14,868 --> 00:02:17,303
Hoods couldn't give
a description, but, uh,

33
00:02:17,371 --> 00:02:20,569
they did mention a growling.

34
00:02:20,641 --> 00:02:21,802
A growling?

35
00:02:21,875 --> 00:02:23,707
It's a rumor; ignore it.

36
00:02:23,777 --> 00:02:26,178
Oswald Cobblepot gets
out of Blackgate tomorrow.

37
00:02:26,246 --> 00:02:28,181
One theory is he's
sending someone

38
00:02:28,248 --> 00:02:30,615
to put the fear of God
into the underworld.

39
00:02:30,684 --> 00:02:33,518
And you choose this moment
to hand in your resignation.

40
00:02:33,587 --> 00:02:34,919
I told you that months ago.

41
00:02:35,188 --> 00:02:36,349
That's not the point.

42
00:02:36,423 --> 00:02:38,756
Look, things are
unstable. I-Isn't there, uh,

43
00:02:38,825 --> 00:02:40,418
uh, some break-in

44
00:02:40,494 --> 00:02:42,827
at a government warehouse
that you guys haven't solved yet?

45
00:02:42,896 --> 00:02:44,626
Yeah, 'cause the
Feds won't tell us squat.

46
00:02:44,698 --> 00:02:47,224
I'm not looking for excuses!

47
00:02:48,435 --> 00:02:51,633
Look... you mean
something to this city.

48
00:02:51,705 --> 00:02:52,705
You can't quit.

49
00:02:53,840 --> 00:02:55,206
Not now.

50
00:02:55,275 --> 00:02:56,868
Because of Wayne Tower.

51
00:02:56,943 --> 00:02:58,755
Bruce Wayne is returning
home for the first time

52
00:02:58,779 --> 00:03:00,179
in a decade for its opening.

53
00:03:00,247 --> 00:03:03,308
The new Wayne Tower
represents hope for Gotham.

54
00:03:03,917 --> 00:03:07,786
So, yeah... I need you.

55
00:03:09,790 --> 00:03:13,386
Mayor James... I
told you I would stay

56
00:03:13,460 --> 00:03:15,895
until after the Wayne inaugural.

57
00:03:16,930 --> 00:03:19,263
Then I'm done.

58
00:03:23,203 --> 00:03:24,398
If you'll excuse me,

59
00:03:24,471 --> 00:03:26,667
I have a fund-raiser I
have to get ready for.

60
00:03:27,240 --> 00:03:28,936
Good day, gentlemen.

61
00:03:29,576 --> 00:03:30,737
BULLOCK: Jim.

62
00:03:31,812 --> 00:03:34,281
I've had ten years, Harv.

63
00:03:34,347 --> 00:03:36,441
It's time for someone
else to have a chance.

64
00:03:36,516 --> 00:03:38,951
And you wait for Bruce to
come back to hang it up?

65
00:03:39,219 --> 00:03:40,881
That's a coincidence?

66
00:03:41,822 --> 00:03:43,984
I'm late. I have
to meet Barbara.

67
00:03:44,257 --> 00:03:45,350
Yeah.

68
00:03:45,859 --> 00:03:47,327
The queen of Gotham.

69
00:03:48,695 --> 00:03:49,822
Tell me something.

70
00:03:49,896 --> 00:03:52,456
Why didn't I buy up half
of Gotham on the cheap

71
00:03:52,532 --> 00:03:53,898
after reunification?

72
00:03:53,967 --> 00:03:56,436
Become a tycoon. Hmm?

73
00:03:57,270 --> 00:03:59,899
Give a kiss to the little
one from Uncle Harv.

74
00:04:00,474 --> 00:04:02,409
Will do.

75
00:04:02,476 --> 00:04:04,809
(door opens)

76
00:04:06,880 --> 00:04:08,576
GORDON: Hey, slugger.

77
00:04:08,648 --> 00:04:10,776
Daddy!

78
00:04:10,851 --> 00:04:11,944
(speaking indistinctly)

79
00:04:12,018 --> 00:04:13,953
- Just do it.
- Yes, ma'am.

80
00:04:16,289 --> 00:04:18,417
Hi, sweetheart.

81
00:04:19,726 --> 00:04:22,389
So... did you hear from Bruce?

82
00:04:22,996 --> 00:04:24,396
No.

83
00:04:24,464 --> 00:04:26,365
Ten years and not a word.

84
00:04:26,433 --> 00:04:29,267
But I'm assuming he'll be at the
gala for Wayne Tower tomorrow.

85
00:04:29,336 --> 00:04:31,635
I want to see the look
on his face when I tell him,

86
00:04:31,705 --> 00:04:34,004
in three months he won't
have the tallest building

87
00:04:34,274 --> 00:04:35,708
in Gotham anymore.

88
00:04:36,643 --> 00:04:38,043
Hmm.

89
00:04:39,579 --> 00:04:40,579
Think he'll recognize you

90
00:04:40,647 --> 00:04:42,616
with that caterpillar
on your top lip?

91
00:04:44,417 --> 00:04:46,283
(chuckles)

92
00:04:46,353 --> 00:04:47,844
Okay, munchkin,
I love you. (kisses)

93
00:04:47,921 --> 00:04:49,913
Don't let her stay up too late.

94
00:04:55,028 --> 00:04:56,462
Ice cream?

95
00:04:56,530 --> 00:04:58,362
Yeah.

96
00:05:00,600 --> 00:05:02,535
(lock buzzes, latch clicks)

97
00:05:02,602 --> 00:05:04,537
(indistinct chatter)

98
00:05:10,410 --> 00:05:11,708
Bruce is back.

99
00:05:11,778 --> 00:05:12,778
(chuckles)

100
00:05:14,681 --> 00:05:16,013
Big deal.

101
00:05:18,051 --> 00:05:20,350
I knew him.

102
00:05:20,420 --> 00:05:23,049
Back in the day.

103
00:05:23,323 --> 00:05:25,952
Saved Gotham together.

104
00:05:28,495 --> 00:05:31,021
(gasps) Oswald's being freed?

105
00:05:31,798 --> 00:05:33,323
Hey!

106
00:05:33,400 --> 00:05:35,096
I've been in here ten years!

107
00:05:35,368 --> 00:05:36,961
Ten years!

108
00:05:37,037 --> 00:05:40,007
I deserve to read the
newspaper, you mouth breather!

109
00:05:41,675 --> 00:05:43,109
(chuckles)

110
00:05:44,778 --> 00:05:46,508
Hey! Hey!

111
00:05:47,113 --> 00:05:48,113
Hey!

112
00:05:50,116 --> 00:05:52,881
Do you know who that is?

113
00:05:56,690 --> 00:05:59,387
Jeremiah Valeska.

114
00:06:00,427 --> 00:06:02,020
And yeah...

115
00:06:02,095 --> 00:06:04,621
he's been a
vegetable for a decade.

116
00:06:04,698 --> 00:06:05,996
Can't think. Can't feel.

117
00:06:06,066 --> 00:06:07,967
But he is

118
00:06:08,034 --> 00:06:10,026
a legend.

119
00:06:10,103 --> 00:06:13,665
And if you're gonna
screw with a legend...

120
00:06:21,715 --> 00:06:24,378
do it properly. (chuckling)

121
00:06:27,120 --> 00:06:28,986
This never gets old. (chuckles)

122
00:06:29,055 --> 00:06:31,047
(alarm ringing)

123
00:06:31,124 --> 00:06:33,116
(inmates screaming)

124
00:06:41,501 --> 00:06:43,527
Hey, buddy, I got
something for you.

125
00:06:43,603 --> 00:06:44,730
Hey!

126
00:06:44,804 --> 00:06:45,982
What are you doing?
Where are you taking me?

127
00:06:46,006 --> 00:06:47,006
Come on.

128
00:06:56,850 --> 00:06:58,978
NURSE: Out of the way.

129
00:07:16,469 --> 00:07:17,937
Whoa.

130
00:07:18,004 --> 00:07:19,996
Yup. It was time to admit it.

131
00:07:20,073 --> 00:07:22,201
I was trying
something. It didn't work.

132
00:07:24,511 --> 00:07:26,446
You liked it, right?

133
00:07:26,880 --> 00:07:28,212
Totally.

134
00:07:29,082 --> 00:07:30,710
At least now Bruce
will recognize you.

135
00:07:30,784 --> 00:07:32,946
Hmm. That's very funny.

136
00:07:36,122 --> 00:07:38,182
I wonder how much he's changed.

137
00:07:38,458 --> 00:07:40,791
Well, it's been ten
years. I'd imagine a lot.

138
00:07:40,860 --> 00:07:42,488
Well, we haven't.

139
00:07:42,562 --> 00:07:44,463
I'm still a doctor.
You're still a cop.

140
00:07:44,531 --> 00:07:47,023
Mm. Not for long.

141
00:07:49,235 --> 00:07:51,795
Are you having second
thoughts about leaving?

142
00:07:52,672 --> 00:07:54,072
Well...

143
00:07:54,140 --> 00:07:56,200
I'm all for it.

144
00:07:56,476 --> 00:07:58,172
But I know how much
this job means to you.

145
00:07:59,012 --> 00:08:01,538
And how much the city
looks to you. It always has.

146
00:08:01,614 --> 00:08:03,583
Well, that's just it.

147
00:08:04,017 --> 00:08:06,816
I was hoping Gotham
would outgrow me.

148
00:08:07,854 --> 00:08:09,880
But it hasn't exactly happened.

149
00:08:09,956 --> 00:08:11,891
No one's stepped forward.

150
00:08:14,160 --> 00:08:16,129
Well, maybe you
need to step down

151
00:08:16,196 --> 00:08:18,597
to allow someone to step up.

152
00:08:19,632 --> 00:08:22,261
(sighs) Jim Gordon.

153
00:08:22,902 --> 00:08:24,564
Clean-shaven man of leisure.

154
00:08:24,637 --> 00:08:25,637
(chuckles)

155
00:08:27,007 --> 00:08:28,908
(chuckles)

156
00:08:31,711 --> 00:08:33,236
Ten years.

157
00:08:34,881 --> 00:08:37,248
I wonder what Bruce
will think of Selina.

158
00:08:38,251 --> 00:08:41,653
<i>She's become quite
the it girl around town.</i>

159
00:08:42,922 --> 00:08:45,824
(beeping)

160
00:09:08,848 --> 00:09:10,817
♪♪♪♪

161
00:09:28,134 --> 00:09:30,126
♪♪♪♪

162
00:09:58,631 --> 00:10:00,122
(gasps)

163
00:10:08,641 --> 00:10:10,371
(siren wailing in distance)

164
00:10:17,617 --> 00:10:19,347
(indistinct chatter)

165
00:10:23,389 --> 00:10:26,291
So they have no idea when
Nygma actually escaped?

166
00:10:26,359 --> 00:10:28,123
He wasn't in his
cell this morning.

167
00:10:28,194 --> 00:10:29,394
This is where the guard lives.

168
00:10:29,629 --> 00:10:31,757
The one that didn't
show for work.

169
00:10:31,831 --> 00:10:33,732
All right. I got it.

170
00:10:33,800 --> 00:10:35,666
Stay here in case
something else comes in.

171
00:10:35,735 --> 00:10:36,896
All right.

172
00:10:43,743 --> 00:10:45,644
(car horns honking in distance)

173
00:10:50,416 --> 00:10:52,647
GCPD.

174
00:10:55,889 --> 00:10:57,255
No! Okay. Okay...

175
00:10:57,323 --> 00:11:00,725
Shut up! Talk to him.

176
00:11:00,793 --> 00:11:03,388
(grunting)

177
00:11:04,664 --> 00:11:06,132
This is Detective Bullock.

178
00:11:06,199 --> 00:11:08,862
(breath trembling)

179
00:11:08,935 --> 00:11:10,335
You understand?

180
00:11:10,403 --> 00:11:11,871
Oh, my God.

181
00:11:11,938 --> 00:11:14,066
You understand
what you have to do?

182
00:11:15,175 --> 00:11:16,404
Oh, my God.

183
00:11:16,676 --> 00:11:17,700
I don't have a choice!

184
00:11:17,777 --> 00:11:19,439
(gunshot) (body thuds)

185
00:11:29,055 --> 00:11:30,990
(door opens)

186
00:11:42,101 --> 00:11:44,002
What the hell happened, Harvey?

187
00:11:44,737 --> 00:11:46,797
What did Harper say?

188
00:11:47,874 --> 00:11:49,900
I want to hear it from you.

189
00:11:50,376 --> 00:11:52,971
We, uh, tracked down
this Arkham guard

190
00:11:53,046 --> 00:11:55,811
we thought maybe
helped Nygma escape.

191
00:11:55,882 --> 00:11:57,475
I shot him.

192
00:11:57,750 --> 00:11:59,343
End of story.

193
00:12:00,820 --> 00:12:02,152
You're confessing...

194
00:12:02,222 --> 00:12:04,851
to killing an unarmed
suspect in cold blood.

195
00:12:04,924 --> 00:12:06,415
That's what happened.

196
00:12:07,160 --> 00:12:08,856
You got to let it go.

197
00:12:08,928 --> 00:12:10,920
Harvey, I don't
know if you think

198
00:12:10,997 --> 00:12:13,762
you're protecting
yourself or someone else,

199
00:12:13,833 --> 00:12:15,153
but you need to
change your story.

200
00:12:15,201 --> 00:12:17,033
Otherwise you're
going to Blackgate.

201
00:12:17,103 --> 00:12:20,039
And you know what
happens to cops in Blackgate.

202
00:12:22,342 --> 00:12:24,971
That's what happened.

203
00:12:25,044 --> 00:12:27,775
So let it go.

204
00:12:27,847 --> 00:12:29,782
(indistinct chatter)

205
00:12:42,829 --> 00:12:45,128
All right, first things first.

206
00:12:45,198 --> 00:12:47,895
Whoever here doesn't believe
Harvey Bullock is innocent

207
00:12:47,967 --> 00:12:49,902
can leave right now.

208
00:12:55,208 --> 00:12:56,369
Good.

209
00:12:57,110 --> 00:12:58,976
(sighs) You think
Nygma's behind this?

210
00:12:59,045 --> 00:13:02,311
Maybe. But he's been
inside Arkham for ten years.

211
00:13:02,382 --> 00:13:04,093
It's not like he suddenly
decided to break out.

212
00:13:04,117 --> 00:13:06,382
He had help. ALVAREZ:
Penguin gets released today.

213
00:13:06,452 --> 00:13:07,852
You think...?

214
00:13:07,920 --> 00:13:10,014
Yeah. Put a tail on him.

215
00:13:10,556 --> 00:13:12,286
In the meantime, I
want every other cop

216
00:13:12,358 --> 00:13:14,327
in this city on the hunt
for Edward Nygma.

217
00:13:14,394 --> 00:13:15,919
We looked into the dead guard.

218
00:13:15,995 --> 00:13:18,089
He used to be associated
with a southside gang.

219
00:13:18,164 --> 00:13:19,928
Got an address.
An old warehouse.

220
00:13:19,999 --> 00:13:21,143
All right. You
and I will hit it.

221
00:13:21,167 --> 00:13:23,864
Rest of you have
your orders. Let's go.

222
00:13:23,936 --> 00:13:25,871
(rat squeaking)

223
00:13:29,942 --> 00:13:31,535
(gasps)

224
00:13:31,811 --> 00:13:34,178
(panting)

225
00:13:35,982 --> 00:13:37,883
(echoing): Hello?!

226
00:13:38,818 --> 00:13:41,014
Anybody?!

227
00:13:41,988 --> 00:13:43,854
Anybody!

228
00:14:02,375 --> 00:14:05,209
"Dear Ed, my old friend.

229
00:14:05,278 --> 00:14:07,577
"Half of Gotham
thinks you a madman.

230
00:14:07,847 --> 00:14:10,407
"The other half
has forgotten you.

231
00:14:11,184 --> 00:14:13,847
It's time to remind
them who the Riddler is."

232
00:14:15,455 --> 00:14:18,391
"I've given you all you
need. Follow the instructions.

233
00:14:18,458 --> 00:14:19,585
Oswald."

234
00:14:28,501 --> 00:14:30,265
(laughing)

235
00:14:34,040 --> 00:14:36,168
Oswald...

236
00:14:36,242 --> 00:14:38,370
what are you planning?

237
00:14:43,649 --> 00:14:45,982
♪♪♪♪

238
00:15:04,904 --> 00:15:07,135
♪♪♪♪

239
00:15:11,310 --> 00:15:13,245
(clamoring)

240
00:15:23,289 --> 00:15:26,623
Mr. Cobblepot, what's the first
thing you'll do as a free man?

241
00:15:27,560 --> 00:15:30,291
I will lay flowers on the
grave of my beloved mother.

242
00:15:30,363 --> 00:15:33,663
And what of Jim Gordon's
role in your incarceration?

243
00:15:33,933 --> 00:15:36,095
Will you seek revenge?

244
00:15:36,169 --> 00:15:38,138
The best revenge
against Jim Gordon

245
00:15:38,204 --> 00:15:41,936
will be a life spent
serving the city I love.

246
00:15:48,581 --> 00:15:49,947
What do you say, young man?

247
00:15:50,016 --> 00:15:51,245
How'd you like an exclusive?

248
00:15:51,317 --> 00:15:52,410
- Yeah, sure.
- Yeah.

249
00:15:52,485 --> 00:15:54,249
(reporters clamoring)

250
00:15:57,256 --> 00:15:59,191
Your jacket and hat.

251
00:15:59,258 --> 00:16:00,658
What?

252
00:16:00,726 --> 00:16:02,217
Now!

253
00:16:09,235 --> 00:16:11,170
(liquid dripping)

254
00:16:26,752 --> 00:16:28,744
(echoing): GCPD!

255
00:16:33,359 --> 00:16:35,191
GCPD.

256
00:16:37,196 --> 00:16:39,028
HARPER: <i>This is the place.</i>

257
00:16:43,069 --> 00:16:45,231
HARPER: <i>Good God.</i>

258
00:16:45,304 --> 00:16:48,035
GORDON: <i>Did your lead
say anything about this?</i>

259
00:16:48,107 --> 00:16:50,576
HARPER: <i>About a
gangland bloodbath?</i>

260
00:16:51,277 --> 00:16:52,277
<i>No.</i>

261
00:16:53,479 --> 00:16:55,311
What the hell is going on?

262
00:16:57,617 --> 00:16:59,415
<i>GORDON: Someone's
covering their tracks.</i>

263
00:17:00,386 --> 00:17:01,386
<i>There was a break-in</i>

264
00:17:01,454 --> 00:17:03,320
<i>in a government
warehouse last week.</i>

265
00:17:03,756 --> 00:17:06,692
Those crates have
U.S. Army markings.

266
00:17:06,759 --> 00:17:08,455
(loud clatter)

267
00:17:09,362 --> 00:17:10,625
Find the back stairs.

268
00:17:19,505 --> 00:17:21,235
GCPD!

269
00:17:24,210 --> 00:17:26,042
I know you're here.

270
00:17:27,346 --> 00:17:28,575
Show yourself.

271
00:17:29,448 --> 00:17:31,349
DISTORTED VOICE:
<i>I am not your enemy.</i>

272
00:17:51,637 --> 00:17:53,148
DISTORTED VOICE:
<i>Don't touch the bodies.</i>

273
00:17:53,172 --> 00:17:54,731
Don't move!

274
00:17:56,475 --> 00:17:58,103
Grenade!

275
00:17:58,844 --> 00:18:01,541
♪♪♪♪

276
00:18:31,577 --> 00:18:32,577
HARPER: Okay, thanks.

277
00:18:32,645 --> 00:18:35,114
(siren chirps outside)

278
00:18:35,848 --> 00:18:38,647
Bomb squad said the
bodies were rigged with C-4.

279
00:18:38,718 --> 00:18:40,414
Whoever that was
saved our lives.

280
00:18:40,886 --> 00:18:42,514
Suggesting...

281
00:18:42,588 --> 00:18:44,420
that he wasn't the
one that killed them.

282
00:18:44,490 --> 00:18:46,891
Could be he's hunting the
same person we're hunting.

283
00:18:47,560 --> 00:18:49,188
Whoever's really
behind all this.

284
00:18:49,261 --> 00:18:51,753
- You thinking
he's on our side?
- Yeah, maybe.

285
00:18:51,831 --> 00:18:53,322
That C-4 has to have been

286
00:18:53,399 --> 00:18:55,493
what was stolen from the
government warehouse.

287
00:18:55,568 --> 00:18:57,764
Which means most
of it's still missing.

288
00:18:57,837 --> 00:19:00,636
Just got a call. Mayor
James vanished,

289
00:19:00,706 --> 00:19:02,402
and our tail lost Penguin.

290
00:19:02,908 --> 00:19:04,536
Sir, what the hell is going on?

291
00:19:05,144 --> 00:19:07,238
First Nygma, now Penguin.

292
00:19:08,180 --> 00:19:09,671
Keep it simple.

293
00:19:10,783 --> 00:19:13,446
Imagine all that C-4.

294
00:19:13,886 --> 00:19:16,685
What's the biggest target
in Gotham right now?

295
00:19:16,756 --> 00:19:19,351
Double security
for tonight's event.

296
00:19:19,425 --> 00:19:22,793
I have to talk to Bruce
Wayne and Alfred Pennyworth.

297
00:19:30,703 --> 00:19:32,501
Hello, old friend.

298
00:19:32,571 --> 00:19:34,335
- Oswald...
- One more word,

299
00:19:34,407 --> 00:19:37,707
and I will put a bullet
in you here and now.

300
00:19:37,777 --> 00:19:39,268
Drive.

301
00:19:42,615 --> 00:19:44,311
(engine starts)

302
00:19:47,219 --> 00:19:48,312
Oswald...

303
00:19:48,387 --> 00:19:51,186
Don't talk!

304
00:19:51,257 --> 00:19:53,419
Turn around!

305
00:19:55,194 --> 00:19:56,890
Remember when
we stood here, Jim,

306
00:19:56,962 --> 00:19:59,295
all those years ago?

307
00:19:59,365 --> 00:20:02,426
Don Falcone wanted you
to shoot me. You refused.

308
00:20:02,902 --> 00:20:05,428
Now don't you wish
you had done it?

309
00:20:05,971 --> 00:20:08,634
Everyone will know you did this.

310
00:20:08,708 --> 00:20:10,199
(laughs quietly)

311
00:20:10,276 --> 00:20:11,710
Let them!

312
00:20:11,777 --> 00:20:16,875
We both know that this
has been a long time coming.

313
00:20:17,483 --> 00:20:19,475
Our story is...

314
00:20:19,552 --> 00:20:21,817
over, old friend.

315
00:20:21,887 --> 00:20:23,913
You want to kill me, fine.

316
00:20:24,623 --> 00:20:27,718
But there's no need to
attack the Wayne gala.

317
00:20:29,328 --> 00:20:30,887
What are you talking about?

318
00:20:30,963 --> 00:20:33,330
Breaking Nygma out of Arkham.

319
00:20:33,399 --> 00:20:34,867
The attacks on the gangs.

320
00:20:34,934 --> 00:20:36,411
What do you think,
you're gonna be able

321
00:20:36,435 --> 00:20:39,337
to destroy Wayne Tower
and no one's gonna notice?

322
00:20:40,439 --> 00:20:42,874
I don't know what
you're talking about.

323
00:20:43,576 --> 00:20:45,568
You and I stood
shoulder to shoulder

324
00:20:45,644 --> 00:20:48,910
on those barricades,
ready to die for this city.

325
00:20:50,282 --> 00:20:51,443
Six months later,

326
00:20:51,517 --> 00:20:54,544
you locked me up like an animal!

327
00:20:55,020 --> 00:20:57,615
This begins and ends

328
00:20:57,690 --> 00:21:00,489
with you and me!

329
00:21:01,827 --> 00:21:03,921
You're telling the truth.

330
00:21:04,697 --> 00:21:07,599
Goodbye, Jim.

331
00:21:07,666 --> 00:21:09,464
(cocks pistol) Turn around!

332
00:21:09,935 --> 00:21:12,404
You know, you made a mistake
bringing me out to this pier.

333
00:21:12,471 --> 00:21:14,337
Don't talk!

334
00:21:14,406 --> 00:21:16,307
Or maybe you just
have a short memory.

335
00:21:16,375 --> 00:21:17,536
(gasping)

336
00:21:21,280 --> 00:21:24,546
(screaming)

337
00:21:29,789 --> 00:21:32,452
<i>♪♪ Blood-filled ♪♪</i>

338
00:21:32,525 --> 00:21:36,553
(indistinct chatter)
<i>♪♪ Jewel of life ♪♪</i>

339
00:21:40,499 --> 00:21:43,833
So, this is Bruce's new Gotham.

340
00:21:43,903 --> 00:21:45,804
I like the old one.

341
00:21:47,673 --> 00:21:49,733
Selina?

342
00:21:50,910 --> 00:21:52,845
How wonderful to see you again.

343
00:21:52,912 --> 00:21:54,972
It's been far, far too long.

344
00:21:55,681 --> 00:21:57,343
Where is he?

345
00:21:57,416 --> 00:21:59,416
Well, I-I'm afraid travels
abroad haven't increased

346
00:21:59,485 --> 00:22:02,353
Master Bruce's respect
for punctuality, Miss Kyle.

347
00:22:03,022 --> 00:22:05,753
I came here to tell him
to stop spying on me.

348
00:22:06,659 --> 00:22:08,059
I don't understand.

349
00:22:08,327 --> 00:22:09,454
I was out the other night

350
00:22:09,528 --> 00:22:11,053
and I felt someone watching me.

351
00:22:11,330 --> 00:22:12,730
I know it was Bruce.

352
00:22:12,798 --> 00:22:14,391
Oh, I see, right, well,

353
00:22:14,466 --> 00:22:16,458
that makes perfect sense.

354
00:22:16,535 --> 00:22:18,970
So you come here tonight
dressed to the nines to tell him

355
00:22:19,038 --> 00:22:20,678
that you want nothing
more to do with him.

356
00:22:20,706 --> 00:22:21,750
Is that the kind of gist of it?

357
00:22:21,774 --> 00:22:23,640
He left, Alfred.

358
00:22:23,709 --> 00:22:26,372
Everything we went through,
and one day he's just gone.

359
00:22:26,445 --> 00:22:28,437
He doesn't get to come
back after ten years

360
00:22:28,514 --> 00:22:30,574
and act like nothing's happened.

361
00:22:32,518 --> 00:22:34,510
On this, we absolutely agree.

362
00:22:35,421 --> 00:22:37,083
I do, however, feel
it might be something

363
00:22:37,356 --> 00:22:39,552
that you want to
tell him yourself.

364
00:22:40,059 --> 00:22:42,756
He needs to stay away.

365
00:22:46,632 --> 00:22:50,069
<i>♪♪ Diamond veins ♪♪</i>

366
00:22:50,135 --> 00:22:53,435
<i>♪♪ Running through me... ♪♪</i>

367
00:22:54,039 --> 00:22:56,406
Nygma?

368
00:22:56,475 --> 00:22:57,841
BARBARA: Well, look at you.

369
00:22:58,611 --> 00:23:01,479
I think Bruce is gonna regret
being gone all these years.

370
00:23:02,781 --> 00:23:04,750
Follow me.

371
00:23:04,817 --> 00:23:06,752
(door opens)

372
00:23:06,819 --> 00:23:07,843
(door closes)

373
00:23:07,920 --> 00:23:10,116
NYGMA: Credit to Bruce.

374
00:23:10,389 --> 00:23:13,018
He did not skimp
on the caterers.

375
00:23:14,059 --> 00:23:15,755
Hungry?

376
00:23:15,828 --> 00:23:17,387
(muffled): Uh-uh.

377
00:23:17,463 --> 00:23:19,989
(chuckles) (TV
playing indistinctly)

378
00:23:20,065 --> 00:23:21,863
Your loss.

379
00:23:21,934 --> 00:23:23,732
Not long now.

380
00:23:23,802 --> 00:23:26,738
NEWSWOMAN: <i>Bruce Wayne's first
public appearance in nearly a decade.</i>

381
00:23:26,805 --> 00:23:29,570
(crowd applauding)

382
00:23:29,642 --> 00:23:31,133
Lucius.

383
00:23:31,410 --> 00:23:32,844
Lee.

384
00:23:32,912 --> 00:23:35,006
Heard about Harvey...
How is he? How's Jim?

385
00:23:35,080 --> 00:23:36,080
I don't know.

386
00:23:36,148 --> 00:23:37,844
I was hoping he would be here.

387
00:23:37,917 --> 00:23:40,409
Ah. (clears throat)
Ladies and gentlemen.

388
00:23:40,486 --> 00:23:45,015
Uh, my name is Alfred
Thaddeus Crane Pennyworth.

389
00:23:45,090 --> 00:23:47,992
And I'd very much
like to welcome you

390
00:23:48,060 --> 00:23:50,996
on behalf of Wayne
Enterprises and Bruce Wayne

391
00:23:51,063 --> 00:23:56,092
to the, uh, future... of Gotham.

392
00:23:56,168 --> 00:23:58,660
(on TV): <i>As you know,
ten years ago, the battle...</i>

393
00:23:58,737 --> 00:24:00,933
Oh, come on.

394
00:24:01,006 --> 00:24:03,635
Where is that brat?

395
00:24:04,176 --> 00:24:05,667
BARBARA: Hello, Ed.

396
00:24:07,146 --> 00:24:08,774
Barbara Kean.

397
00:24:09,481 --> 00:24:10,505
In red.

398
00:24:10,582 --> 00:24:11,948
(chuckles)

399
00:24:14,219 --> 00:24:16,484
Oh, no.

400
00:24:16,555 --> 00:24:19,047
Please tell me you
are not here to stop me.

401
00:24:19,858 --> 00:24:21,622
Barbara...

402
00:24:21,694 --> 00:24:24,858
Do you even remember
how amazing you used to be?

403
00:24:24,930 --> 00:24:27,866
Honey, I'm still amazing.

404
00:24:27,933 --> 00:24:30,129
(chuckles) I just made a choice.

405
00:24:32,137 --> 00:24:34,197
You made a choice.

406
00:24:34,473 --> 00:24:37,033
Some of us don't
get to make choices.

407
00:24:37,109 --> 00:24:39,510
I'm The Riddler.

408
00:24:39,578 --> 00:24:42,548
And tonight Gotham
will remember that.

409
00:24:42,614 --> 00:24:44,708
By blowing up this ding-dong?

410
00:24:44,783 --> 00:24:45,944
Didn't you do that already?

411
00:24:46,018 --> 00:24:47,213
It's a callback.

412
00:24:49,488 --> 00:24:51,855
I was waiting for Bruce
to begin his speech.

413
00:24:51,924 --> 00:24:55,793
You know, come
out, present a riddle.

414
00:24:55,861 --> 00:24:58,160
Only Bruce doesn't
seem to want to show.

415
00:24:59,231 --> 00:25:00,859
So I think I'm
gonna have to imp...

416
00:25:01,867 --> 00:25:03,665
(muffled grunting)

417
00:25:03,736 --> 00:25:04,931
(sighs)

418
00:25:05,004 --> 00:25:07,200
BARBARA: Sorry, Ed.

419
00:25:07,940 --> 00:25:09,806
Not tonight.

420
00:25:09,875 --> 00:25:13,073
Wayne Enterprises
will devote itself

421
00:25:13,145 --> 00:25:15,171
to making this future a reality.

422
00:25:15,247 --> 00:25:16,738
(doors bang open)

423
00:25:16,815 --> 00:25:19,808
- Lee.
- (Alfred continues indistinctly)

424
00:25:19,885 --> 00:25:22,047
- THOMPKINS: Jim.
- I'm fine. Evacuate the building.

425
00:25:22,121 --> 00:25:24,920
- Get these people
out of here.
- JAMES: Help!

426
00:25:24,990 --> 00:25:26,515
Gordon!

427
00:25:26,592 --> 00:25:28,891
Help! Gordon!

428
00:25:28,961 --> 00:25:30,657
Gordon, help! (crowd screaming)

429
00:25:30,729 --> 00:25:32,630
This lunatic.

430
00:25:32,698 --> 00:25:34,223
He kidnapped me again.

431
00:25:34,299 --> 00:25:36,097
He tried to blow me up. Again!

432
00:25:36,168 --> 00:25:37,796
But we stopped him.

433
00:25:37,870 --> 00:25:39,202
You're welcome.

434
00:25:39,271 --> 00:25:40,511
Take care of the mayor, please.

435
00:25:40,539 --> 00:25:41,802
Get that thing off of him.

436
00:25:41,874 --> 00:25:43,570
Excuse me.

437
00:25:43,642 --> 00:25:44,786
There were four crates of C-4.

438
00:25:44,810 --> 00:25:46,176
Where are the rest?

439
00:25:46,245 --> 00:25:47,804
That's all he gave me.

440
00:25:47,880 --> 00:25:49,906
- He said Penguin broke him out.
- No.

441
00:25:49,982 --> 00:25:51,542
It wasn't Penguin.
Get him out of there.

442
00:25:51,583 --> 00:25:52,915
What?

443
00:25:52,985 --> 00:25:55,079
Hey! Get off me.

444
00:25:55,154 --> 00:25:56,314
Penguin not's just the patsy.

445
00:25:56,555 --> 00:25:58,080
He's not even the real threat.

446
00:25:58,157 --> 00:25:59,648
Which means there must be...

447
00:26:04,630 --> 00:26:06,599
♪♪♪♪

448
00:26:11,236 --> 00:26:15,037
(beeping)

449
00:26:21,346 --> 00:26:22,871
GORDON: If this bomb goes off

450
00:26:22,948 --> 00:26:25,247
and Wayne Tower falls,
it'll take out other buildings.

451
00:26:25,317 --> 00:26:26,683
A lot of people are gonna die.

452
00:26:26,752 --> 00:26:28,687
You all need to leave right now.

453
00:26:28,754 --> 00:26:30,780
So you can stay? Absolutely not.

454
00:26:30,856 --> 00:26:31,949
It's too late.

455
00:26:32,024 --> 00:26:33,617
We'd never get far enough away.

456
00:26:33,692 --> 00:26:36,594
Ms. Kean is right;
this stops right here.

457
00:26:39,264 --> 00:26:40,789
So how do we defuse it?

458
00:26:40,866 --> 00:26:43,062
We'd have to sever the
connectors to the detonator,

459
00:26:43,135 --> 00:26:44,312
but the bomber
must have hidden it.

460
00:26:44,336 --> 00:26:45,929
The wires go up
inside the model.

461
00:26:46,004 --> 00:26:47,973
It must be in one
of the buildings.

462
00:26:48,040 --> 00:26:49,240
I tracked down a gang today...

463
00:26:49,274 --> 00:26:51,175
They had bomb-making materials,

464
00:26:51,243 --> 00:26:53,007
pictures of buildings.

465
00:26:53,846 --> 00:26:55,314
One in particular:

466
00:26:55,981 --> 00:26:57,176
Gotham Clock Tower.

467
00:26:59,718 --> 00:27:01,653
(alarm ringing)

468
00:27:01,720 --> 00:27:03,655
Let's go.

469
00:27:05,357 --> 00:27:06,723
In here.

470
00:27:09,261 --> 00:27:10,923
(grunts)

471
00:27:10,996 --> 00:27:12,259
Wait, wait, wait.

472
00:27:12,331 --> 00:27:14,232
(beeping)

473
00:27:27,212 --> 00:27:30,944
Wait. This particular
detonator has a gyroscope.

474
00:27:31,016 --> 00:27:34,976
Which means someone will
have to hold it up and steady

475
00:27:35,053 --> 00:27:36,783
while you detach
the wires from below.

476
00:27:36,855 --> 00:27:39,222
I have doctor's
hands, I can do it.

477
00:27:46,064 --> 00:27:48,033
Fine. Lucius.

478
00:27:52,905 --> 00:27:54,771
LUCIUS: All right,
the trigger connection

479
00:27:54,840 --> 00:27:57,105
should be different
than the others.

480
00:27:57,176 --> 00:28:00,305
THOMPKINS: Okay,
I see two green wires.

481
00:28:01,380 --> 00:28:03,815
I'm gonna cut this one.

482
00:28:12,691 --> 00:28:14,455
♪♪♪♪

483
00:28:26,705 --> 00:28:28,833
(beeping)

484
00:28:29,942 --> 00:28:32,173
(sighs) (Barbara sighs)

485
00:28:34,947 --> 00:28:35,990
- The other one. The other one.
- The other one.

486
00:28:36,014 --> 00:28:37,494
- The other one.
- Yes, the other one.

487
00:28:43,455 --> 00:28:46,857
(sighs)

488
00:28:46,925 --> 00:28:48,723
Never doubted you for a minute.

489
00:28:51,964 --> 00:28:53,159
Strange.

490
00:28:53,232 --> 00:28:57,101
We designed a new clock
tower, but this is the old one.

491
00:29:03,041 --> 00:29:04,441
That's the answer.

492
00:29:05,077 --> 00:29:07,444
Who's behind all this, but...

493
00:29:08,413 --> 00:29:09,779
but it's not possible.

494
00:29:09,848 --> 00:29:11,009
HARPER: Sir.

495
00:29:11,083 --> 00:29:13,075
Sir, Nygma's vanished.

496
00:29:13,151 --> 00:29:14,380
There's more.

497
00:29:14,453 --> 00:29:16,253
Mayor James ordered
Bullock sent to Blackgate.

498
00:29:16,321 --> 00:29:17,812
He's about to be moved.

499
00:29:17,889 --> 00:29:19,790
(sirens wailing in distance)

500
00:29:25,764 --> 00:29:29,166
GORDON: Stop! Stop!

501
00:29:29,901 --> 00:29:30,960
The person who framed you,

502
00:29:31,036 --> 00:29:32,213
the one behind Nygma's breakout,

503
00:29:32,237 --> 00:29:33,848
is it who I think it is?
Has he been faking it?

504
00:29:33,872 --> 00:29:36,239
Jim, do not say his name!

505
00:29:36,308 --> 00:29:37,970
Is it Jeremiah Valeska?

506
00:29:39,478 --> 00:29:41,276
(grunts) Harvey.

507
00:29:41,346 --> 00:29:42,939
Check him for a wire! What?

508
00:29:43,015 --> 00:29:45,382
Under his shirt.
Check for a wire.

509
00:29:48,854 --> 00:29:50,134
BULLOCK: Oh, God, it's too late.

510
00:29:51,423 --> 00:29:53,358
He's miked.

511
00:29:53,425 --> 00:29:55,894
Jim, you don't
know what he'll do.

512
00:29:56,962 --> 00:29:59,158
I-I don't know about this.

513
00:29:59,231 --> 00:30:00,961
How much is it again?

514
00:30:01,033 --> 00:30:03,901
ORDERLY: Ten bucks is a
body punch. $20, you get the face.

515
00:30:03,969 --> 00:30:05,232
Stabbing him is a C-note.

516
00:30:05,304 --> 00:30:06,397
Huh.

517
00:30:06,471 --> 00:30:08,235
(grunting)

518
00:30:10,242 --> 00:30:11,505
Bad news, boss.

519
00:30:11,576 --> 00:30:14,273
Our cover's blownskies.

520
00:30:16,548 --> 00:30:18,039
(chuckles softly)

521
00:30:18,116 --> 00:30:19,448
(cackles)

522
00:30:19,518 --> 00:30:20,542
(gasps)

523
00:30:20,819 --> 00:30:22,549
(car horns honking in distance)

524
00:30:24,189 --> 00:30:26,351
(grunts)

525
00:30:26,425 --> 00:30:28,053
OSWALD: Edward Nygma.

526
00:30:28,126 --> 00:30:31,255
It is very good to see you.

527
00:30:31,330 --> 00:30:34,960
Oswald... I thought
you weren't behind this.

528
00:30:35,033 --> 00:30:36,033
I'm not.

529
00:30:36,101 --> 00:30:38,832
But I thought you
might need some help,

530
00:30:38,904 --> 00:30:41,499
and... what else
are friends for?

531
00:30:41,573 --> 00:30:43,098
(chuckles)

532
00:30:43,175 --> 00:30:44,575
You look well.

533
00:30:44,843 --> 00:30:46,903
You, too.

534
00:30:46,978 --> 00:30:48,089
A little thicker in the middle.

535
00:30:48,113 --> 00:30:49,113
(chuckles)

536
00:30:50,515 --> 00:30:52,882
Damn, it's good
to see you, Oswald.

537
00:30:52,951 --> 00:30:54,078
(both chuckling)

538
00:30:55,020 --> 00:30:56,215
(tires screeching)

539
00:30:56,288 --> 00:30:58,382
Wh-What was that? What was that?

540
00:30:58,457 --> 00:31:00,358
(screams)

541
00:31:00,425 --> 00:31:01,425
(crash)

542
00:31:01,493 --> 00:31:03,223
(horn honking)

543
00:31:07,299 --> 00:31:09,564
What the hell was that?!

544
00:31:09,634 --> 00:31:11,569
(coughs)

545
00:31:11,636 --> 00:31:13,537
(whooshing)

546
00:31:15,140 --> 00:31:17,575
(both screaming)

547
00:31:22,314 --> 00:31:24,977
(sirens wailing in distance)

548
00:31:29,020 --> 00:31:32,582
Alfred, when Bruce came
to me the day he got back

549
00:31:32,657 --> 00:31:34,697
and told me what he was
planning, I didn't hesitate.

550
00:31:35,627 --> 00:31:37,323
I believe in what he's doing,

551
00:31:37,396 --> 00:31:39,262
but he's going to
need some help.

552
00:31:40,132 --> 00:31:42,067
Has he thought
about telling Gordon?

553
00:31:43,068 --> 00:31:45,503
Lucius, my old friend,

554
00:31:45,570 --> 00:31:47,730
whoever Bruce decides to
take on this journey with him,

555
00:31:47,906 --> 00:31:49,568
it's his decision.

556
00:31:49,641 --> 00:31:53,305
Our role... is to serve.

557
00:31:54,479 --> 00:31:57,244
(Oswald and Nygma straining)

558
00:31:59,518 --> 00:32:00,918
Down!

559
00:32:00,986 --> 00:32:02,921
- Get me down!
- Aah!

560
00:32:04,523 --> 00:32:06,492
Something happened
tonight, didn't it?

561
00:32:06,558 --> 00:32:07,924
Why won't you tell me?

562
00:32:07,993 --> 00:32:10,428
Because everything
worked out okay, didn't it?

563
00:32:12,097 --> 00:32:14,362
So why are we at your old club?

564
00:32:14,433 --> 00:32:16,299
Because Mommy just
needs to get something.

565
00:32:19,438 --> 00:32:22,101
<i>♪♪ I ♪♪</i>

566
00:32:23,608 --> 00:32:24,940
<i>♪♪ Now, I don't hardly... ♪♪</i>

567
00:32:25,010 --> 00:32:27,172
Wait here, okay?

568
00:32:30,182 --> 00:32:34,483
<i>♪♪ But I think I
could love her ♪♪</i>

569
00:32:37,222 --> 00:32:38,222
Turn around.

570
00:32:38,290 --> 00:32:40,088
<i>♪♪ Crimson and clover ♪♪</i>

571
00:32:40,158 --> 00:32:42,024
Turn around.

572
00:32:42,093 --> 00:32:43,721
I won't ask again.

573
00:32:43,995 --> 00:32:45,395
Surprise.

574
00:32:45,464 --> 00:32:47,660
(grunting)

575
00:32:47,732 --> 00:32:49,291
Easy.

576
00:32:49,367 --> 00:32:51,336
It's just a surprise party.

577
00:32:51,736 --> 00:32:54,205
For you, Barbara Kean,

578
00:32:54,272 --> 00:32:56,434
queen of Gotham,

579
00:32:56,508 --> 00:32:59,740
business titan. How exciting.

580
00:33:00,445 --> 00:33:02,346
But there was another you, I...

581
00:33:02,414 --> 00:33:04,246
I seem to recall.

582
00:33:04,316 --> 00:33:05,375
Wasn't there?

583
00:33:05,450 --> 00:33:07,112
Then again, there was, uh,

584
00:33:07,185 --> 00:33:09,211
another me, too.

585
00:33:09,287 --> 00:33:12,257
Oh, so hard holding
on to what's real. It's...

586
00:33:12,324 --> 00:33:14,122
(grunts) It's enough
to drive you mad.

587
00:33:14,192 --> 00:33:15,192
(chuckles)

588
00:33:16,461 --> 00:33:19,295
(grunting)

589
00:33:19,364 --> 00:33:21,526
No!

590
00:33:21,600 --> 00:33:23,694
BARBARA LEE (screams): Mom!

591
00:33:23,768 --> 00:33:25,703
Cute.

592
00:33:25,770 --> 00:33:27,363
(panting)

593
00:33:27,439 --> 00:33:29,499
She has your eyes.

594
00:33:29,574 --> 00:33:31,167
For now.

595
00:33:31,243 --> 00:33:32,438
No, put me down.

596
00:33:32,511 --> 00:33:34,503
(whimpers) I...

597
00:33:34,579 --> 00:33:36,514
think she...

598
00:33:36,581 --> 00:33:38,709
nicked me, Daddy.

599
00:33:38,783 --> 00:33:40,479
I...

600
00:33:40,552 --> 00:33:42,214
Oh, boy.

601
00:33:42,287 --> 00:33:44,313
Oh, dear me.

602
00:33:44,389 --> 00:33:46,187
My sweet Ecco,

603
00:33:46,258 --> 00:33:48,750
no longer my echo.

604
00:33:49,027 --> 00:33:51,622
There will never
be one like you.

605
00:33:51,696 --> 00:33:53,358
Really?

606
00:33:56,034 --> 00:33:57,730
(chuckles)

607
00:34:00,071 --> 00:34:02,666
But I suppose there
are other fish in the sea.

608
00:34:02,741 --> 00:34:03,741
Let me...

609
00:34:03,808 --> 00:34:05,140
down. (panting)

610
00:34:06,278 --> 00:34:07,610
- Mom!
- Hush,

611
00:34:07,679 --> 00:34:11,172
little Barbaras,
don't say a word.

612
00:34:11,249 --> 00:34:13,343
Now we're going to play a...

613
00:34:13,418 --> 00:34:15,148
little game. (panting)

614
00:34:15,220 --> 00:34:17,212
By now, James Gordon
should have made it

615
00:34:17,289 --> 00:34:18,552
to your apartment.

616
00:34:18,623 --> 00:34:20,717
When he gets here,
I want you to deliver

617
00:34:20,792 --> 00:34:22,385
a message. Okay?

618
00:34:22,460 --> 00:34:23,655
(exhales, sniffles)

619
00:34:23,728 --> 00:34:25,162
Okay?

620
00:34:25,230 --> 00:34:27,131
(giggles)

621
00:34:27,198 --> 00:34:28,689
Okay?

622
00:34:32,170 --> 00:34:33,263
(door opens)

623
00:34:33,338 --> 00:34:34,338
GORDON: Barbara.

624
00:34:36,641 --> 00:34:38,576
I'll call an ambulance.

625
00:34:38,643 --> 00:34:39,643
Barbara.

626
00:34:39,711 --> 00:34:41,771
Barbara.

627
00:34:41,846 --> 00:34:43,314
He took her!

628
00:34:43,381 --> 00:34:45,077
That lunatic took her!

629
00:34:45,150 --> 00:34:47,210
He said you have to
come, and if you don't come,

630
00:34:47,285 --> 00:34:48,344
he's gonna kill her.

631
00:34:48,420 --> 00:34:49,581
Where?

632
00:34:50,388 --> 00:34:53,654
The place where
he was born again.

633
00:34:54,459 --> 00:34:56,121
He means Ace Chemicals.

634
00:34:57,529 --> 00:34:59,691
You promise me.

635
00:35:00,865 --> 00:35:02,731
I'll bring her back.

636
00:35:05,537 --> 00:35:07,472
(door opens)

637
00:35:07,539 --> 00:35:09,201
(door closes)

638
00:35:12,344 --> 00:35:14,711
JEREMIAH: Come
along, Commissioner.

639
00:35:14,779 --> 00:35:16,475
We're waiting.

640
00:35:17,315 --> 00:35:18,408
The party's raging,

641
00:35:18,483 --> 00:35:21,851
but it's well past the
princess's bedtime.

642
00:35:23,688 --> 00:35:25,748
It's funny, being back here.

643
00:35:27,158 --> 00:35:29,457
I can still feel my flesh

644
00:35:30,295 --> 00:35:33,459
sizzle as it melted away.

645
00:35:33,531 --> 00:35:35,124
Burns even now.

646
00:35:35,200 --> 00:35:37,226
Ooh. Oh.

647
00:35:37,302 --> 00:35:38,302
(screams)

648
00:35:39,638 --> 00:35:41,197
I'm here.

649
00:35:41,272 --> 00:35:42,797
Everything's gonna be fine.

650
00:35:42,874 --> 00:35:44,775
You think so?

651
00:35:44,843 --> 00:35:48,302
Personally, I'd say things
are about as far away from fine

652
00:35:48,380 --> 00:35:50,542
as they could possibly
be, Barbara Lee.

653
00:35:50,615 --> 00:35:54,382
What do I know? I did
just spend the last ten years

654
00:35:54,452 --> 00:35:56,421
in the funny farm. (giggles)

655
00:35:56,488 --> 00:35:58,616
What do you want, Jeremiah?

656
00:36:00,759 --> 00:36:03,524
Is there a Jeremiah here?

657
00:36:04,896 --> 00:36:06,694
So what do I call you?

658
00:36:06,765 --> 00:36:07,765
Uh...

659
00:36:07,832 --> 00:36:09,528
I don't know.

660
00:36:09,601 --> 00:36:11,695
Call me... Jack.

661
00:36:11,770 --> 00:36:13,170
Mm, no, no, no,
that's not right.

662
00:36:13,238 --> 00:36:15,298
J-Joseph. John. Jay.

663
00:36:15,373 --> 00:36:16,773
I-I don't know. I just...

664
00:36:16,841 --> 00:36:19,777
I feel something new crawling

665
00:36:19,844 --> 00:36:21,938
from the primordial
ooze that was me.

666
00:36:22,213 --> 00:36:23,579
Something...

667
00:36:23,648 --> 00:36:25,583
beautiful.

668
00:36:26,584 --> 00:36:28,746
How long have you been
pretending to be brain-dead?

669
00:36:28,820 --> 00:36:31,346
How long have <i>you</i>
been pretending?

670
00:36:31,423 --> 00:36:33,517
That's a joke. I know
you're not pretending.

671
00:36:33,591 --> 00:36:35,219
That's far enough, James.

672
00:36:35,960 --> 00:36:37,622
(clucks)

673
00:36:38,463 --> 00:36:41,297
GORDON: But you
still haven't told me.

674
00:36:42,734 --> 00:36:44,293
Why?

675
00:36:45,270 --> 00:36:47,239
Why keep pretending?

676
00:36:48,306 --> 00:36:51,834
I was waiting for
him to come home.

677
00:36:52,577 --> 00:36:55,411
We're bound together, he and I.

678
00:36:56,381 --> 00:36:58,543
It's the one thing I knew
for certain, the one thing

679
00:36:58,616 --> 00:37:00,710
I knew was true.

680
00:37:01,653 --> 00:37:03,315
And then he just...

681
00:37:03,388 --> 00:37:05,721
abandoned us.

682
00:37:06,391 --> 00:37:08,860
Do you know how it
feels to have the one,

683
00:37:08,927 --> 00:37:11,362
the only thing you love

684
00:37:11,429 --> 00:37:12,988
ripped away from you?

685
00:37:14,833 --> 00:37:16,233
It feels like this.

686
00:37:16,301 --> 00:37:17,633
- No!
- (screams)

687
00:37:19,704 --> 00:37:20,899
(laughs)

688
00:37:20,972 --> 00:37:21,972
- (grunts)
- (shouts)

689
00:37:22,240 --> 00:37:23,731
(laughs)

690
00:37:23,808 --> 00:37:25,777
Disappointing as tonight was,

691
00:37:25,844 --> 00:37:27,745
I will say, it is fun carving up

692
00:37:27,812 --> 00:37:29,781
Filet-O-Commissioner. (giggling)

693
00:37:29,848 --> 00:37:32,010
(clang)

694
00:37:33,752 --> 00:37:35,277
Who's there?!

695
00:37:35,353 --> 00:37:36,878
What do you want?!

696
00:37:36,955 --> 00:37:38,287
Show yourself!

697
00:37:40,692 --> 00:37:42,320
Show yourself!

698
00:37:42,393 --> 00:37:44,953
(whooshing)

699
00:37:48,266 --> 00:37:49,325
You.

700
00:37:51,669 --> 00:37:54,298
(Jeremiah laughing)

701
00:37:57,909 --> 00:38:00,811
(laughing)

702
00:38:01,780 --> 00:38:04,045
♪♪♪♪

703
00:38:11,656 --> 00:38:13,852
It's okay. It's all right.

704
00:38:13,925 --> 00:38:16,417
I got you, okay?

705
00:38:31,442 --> 00:38:33,308
So, he comes out of nowhere,

706
00:38:33,378 --> 00:38:36,405
saves you <i>and</i> Barbara Lee,

707
00:38:36,481 --> 00:38:38,382
and just disappears?

708
00:38:38,449 --> 00:38:39,449
Yeah.

709
00:38:39,517 --> 00:38:41,645
So, the dude's on our side?

710
00:38:41,719 --> 00:38:43,881
I think so.

711
00:38:43,955 --> 00:38:46,447
Hey, this old thing.

712
00:38:47,325 --> 00:38:50,693
I thought we, uh, mothballed
this after reunification.

713
00:38:50,762 --> 00:38:52,060
I had 'em dig it out

714
00:38:52,330 --> 00:38:53,798
for old times' sake.

715
00:38:53,865 --> 00:38:55,993
I sent a note to Wayne Manor.

716
00:38:56,067 --> 00:38:59,435
I thought Bruce might want
to be here when we light it.

717
00:39:07,579 --> 00:39:08,911
Good evening, gentlemen.

718
00:39:09,581 --> 00:39:12,745
Master Bruce sends
his profound apologies.

719
00:39:12,817 --> 00:39:14,945
He's otherwise engaged.

720
00:39:15,587 --> 00:39:17,886
He's been busy a lot
since he came back.

721
00:39:17,956 --> 00:39:19,424
Yes, indeed.

722
00:39:19,924 --> 00:39:22,450
And I hear that you're retiring.

723
00:39:24,896 --> 00:39:25,896
I may stick around

724
00:39:25,964 --> 00:39:28,456
a while yet.

725
00:39:30,768 --> 00:39:33,033
♪♪♪♪

726
00:40:00,865 --> 00:40:02,595
You're there, aren't you?

727
00:40:11,910 --> 00:40:13,936
Do you have any
idea what you did...

728
00:40:16,547 --> 00:40:18,675
just leaving?

729
00:40:21,986 --> 00:40:24,615
You were all I had.

730
00:40:26,024 --> 00:40:29,426
And I know you
wanted to protect me.

731
00:40:30,895 --> 00:40:32,591
But I didn't want
to be protected.

732
00:40:32,664 --> 00:40:34,929
I wanted you.

733
00:40:38,703 --> 00:40:40,672
Say something.

734
00:40:40,738 --> 00:40:43,105
(quietly): Say something.

735
00:40:44,776 --> 00:40:46,972
There was no other way, Selina.

736
00:40:48,680 --> 00:40:50,649
I had to go.

737
00:40:54,052 --> 00:40:56,715
So what happens now?

738
00:40:57,455 --> 00:40:59,117
I don't know.

739
00:41:00,024 --> 00:41:02,926
But I'll never leave
Gotham again.

740
00:41:03,728 --> 00:41:05,663
Return the diamond.

741
00:41:06,230 --> 00:41:08,131
(whooshing)

742
00:41:15,139 --> 00:41:16,732
Like hell.

743
00:41:23,848 --> 00:41:25,612
"Gotham is mine."
That's what he said.

744
00:41:25,683 --> 00:41:26,912
I was there, Oswald.

745
00:41:26,985 --> 00:41:29,580
I did not spend ten
years in Blackgate

746
00:41:29,654 --> 00:41:32,488
to give my city to a
man dressed like a bat!

747
00:41:32,557 --> 00:41:33,752
Yes!

748
00:41:34,993 --> 00:41:37,121
(grunts) Go!

749
00:41:42,800 --> 00:41:44,564
We have to find out who he is

750
00:41:44,635 --> 00:41:46,604
and show him
that this is <i>our</i> city!

751
00:41:46,671 --> 00:41:47,671
Agreed.

752
00:41:47,739 --> 00:41:48,832
(gasps)

753
00:41:59,717 --> 00:42:01,549
Tomorrow?

754
00:42:03,021 --> 00:42:05,047
Tomorrow.

755
00:42:14,532 --> 00:42:15,966
Yet in the darkness,

756
00:42:17,035 --> 00:42:19,027
there will be light.

757
00:42:21,305 --> 00:42:22,745
That's what you
promised Master Bruce

758
00:42:22,807 --> 00:42:24,639
all those years
ago in the alley.

759
00:42:26,544 --> 00:42:28,809
You saved him.

760
00:42:29,680 --> 00:42:31,672
Gave him hope.

761
00:42:36,320 --> 00:42:38,653
Holy Mother.

762
00:42:45,196 --> 00:42:48,724
♪♪♪♪

763
00:42:55,039 --> 00:42:56,701
Who is he?

764
00:42:59,944 --> 00:43:02,106
A friend.

765
00:43:02,180 --> 00:43:04,615
♪♪♪♪
